    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d584">

                <pb facs="0698" n="578" sameAs="frus:frus1931v02/pg578"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">815.00 Revolutions/165: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Honduras</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Lay</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Tegucigalpa</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1931-06-05T16:00:00-06:00">June 5, 1931—4
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 9:10 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>115. Information just received from United Fruit Company agent Castillo that
                    Ferrera reported advancing northerly direction toward point on railway 50 miles
                    southeast of Puerto Castillo. Company concentrating railroad rolling stock
                    Castillo. Above repeated to Salvador, Guatemala and Managua for Comsperon.</p>
                <pb facs="0699" n="579" xml:id="pg579"/>
                <p>Company has been obliged to deliver at Castillo gasoline and oil for plane
                    mentioned in my telegram 113, June 3, 3 p.m., under orders from the President. I
                    am flying tomorrow to Castillo thence if situation favorable in U. S. S. <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Richmond</hi> to Ceiba and Tela returning here probably
                    June 12.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Lay</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
